-- title:
--   Witt vectors of k surject onto O^{nr}/π^N with kernel r^N
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime. Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, let $\pi \in \mathcal O$ be irreducible, assume $\mathcal O$ is adically complete for the ideal $(\pi)$, that the quotient $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements, and that the ideal generated by the image of $r$ in $\mathcal O$ equals $(\pi)$. Let $O^{nr}$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, such that every $x \in O^{nr}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo that ideal, and every monic polynomial over $O^{nr}$ of positive degree has a root modulo that ideal. Let $k$ be a perfect field of characteristic $r$, and let $\rho_1 : O^{nr} \to k$ be a surjective ring homomorphism whose kernel is the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$. The conclusion is that for every natural number $N$ there exists a ring homomorphism $f : W_r(k) \to O^{nr}/(\pi^N)$ (the ideal being generated by the $N$-th power of the image of $\pi$) such that: if $N > 0$, then for all $x \in O^{nr}$ and $w \in W_r(k)$ with $x \bmod \pi^N = f(w)$ one has $\rho_1(x)$ equal to the constant Witt coefficient of $w$; $f$ is surjective; and $f(w) = 0$ holds exactly when $w$ lies in the ideal of $W_r(k)$ generated by $r^N$.
--
--   This is the level-wise comparison identifying $O^{nr}/(\pi^N)$ with $W(k)/r^N W(k)$ for the unramified coefficient ring $O^{nr}$ over an absolutely unramified base $(\mathcal O,\pi)$ with residue field of $r$ elements; the homomorphism comes from the universal property of Witt vectors over a perfect field applied to a quotient with nilpotent residual kernel ([`WittVector.existsUnique_ringHom_comp_eq_constantCoeff_of_isNilpotent_ker`](thm.html#WittVector.existsUnique_ringHom_comp_eq_constantCoeff_of_isNilpotent_ker)). It feeds the construction of the coefficient ring used in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd formal uniformisation, being cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.existsUnique_algHom_comp_eq_of_surjective_of_isNilpotent`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.existsUnique_algHom_comp_eq_of_surjective_of_isNilpotent).
